to-be-incorporated-into-paper-140 : List Word
to-be-incorporated-into-paper-140 = unlines (cons "In hyperactivity's language as the repository implements it: **Commands.** `#check e : T`, `#same a = b` (equal readings, at a type when either side has one)," (cons "`#show e`, `#observe n e` (a codata value unfolded n levels), `#usage f`, `#trusted`, `#safe f`," (cons "`#jit f [using t…]` (“Programs about programs, and the compiler” in “The language as implemented” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)), `#key d`, `#names K`, `#history d`, `#unbind d`, `#gc`, `#run s`," (cons "`#input x` and `#supply x = e` (“Inputs” in “The language as implemented” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)), `#fail` before a declaration or command (it must be" (cons "rejected). A name is bound once: a second definition, data type or constructor of the same name" (cons (quoted (cons "is refused, and so is a clause no case reaches. `import " (cons "file.cub" (cons "` loads a module" nil)))) (cons "once. Results and failures print in the surface syntax, a failed check with its declaration's" (cons "`file:line` and the term at fault. `--serve` after the files reads blocks of declarations from" (cons "the standard input, each ended by a line `.`, and answers each as a file would be answered," (cons "ending the reply with `.` (a fatal error ends the request, not the machine). `#retract f` hides" (cons "the checked definition `f` (or a data, codata or record type with its constructors, fields and" (cons "projections) so the name can be declared again; what was checked against the old one keeps it (a" (cons "global is referenced by its index), later declarations see the new one. `#type e` prints the type" (cons "the checker infers for `e`, `#scope` the names in scope, `#where f` where `f` was declared." (cons "`--read` before the files checks what they declare without performing what acts on the world:" (cons "`#run`, `#build` and `#build-loop` are read (their uses recorded) and not performed. `#uses` prints every declaration read so far, one line each: its position, the names it declares" (cons "(those generated from it included) and the positions of the declarations it mentions" (cons "(the store keeps them per name, which `hyperactive why` and `unexplained` read). `CUBICAL_PROFILE=1` prints the run's profile, `=show` the profile from the last `#show`. The core forms the language compiles to" (cons "(`(lam x b)`, `(elim P e ((c x) b))`, …) are still read from files of other extensions, and" (cons "`--print FILE` prints such a file in the surface syntax." nil))))))))))))))))))))
